# One run's evidence, not the repository's state.
#
# A platform evidence file records what happened on ONE runner at ONE commit.
# Committing it would let a stale green file outlive the code it described --
# and build/acceptance/report.py reads these files to decide Phase 5
# eligibility, so a committed one is a way to make the gate lie.
#
# In CI they arrive as job artifacts, downloaded into evidence/ by
# first-wave-acceptance. Locally they are whatever your last `make ci-*` run
# produced.
evidence/
logs/
